  "rationale": "Throughput >= 1 MSPS rules out iterative (1 result every N+3 cycles; even at 150 MHz, N=10 gives ~13.6 MSPS which is fine, but area is higher due to barrel shifters and FSM overhead vs pipelined). Actually iterative could work throughput-wise, but pipelined_m and unrolled_k are more area-efficient for 1/cycle or near-1/cycle operation. I excluded iterative because its shared datapath with barrel shifters typically has higher LUT count than the pipelined variants for equivalent accuracy, and the spec prioritizes area minimization. pipelined_m is the primary focus because it offers 1/cycle throughput with reduced FFs (register every m stages). unrolled_k is included as a strong area competitor since it uses a shared datapath with fewer registers. pipelined is included as a baseline to establish the Pareto front. Data width 12-16 and n_iter 10-14 are chosen to satisfy max_abs_err <= 2^-10 with margin while keeping area low. angle_guard 0-2 and frac_guard 0-2 provide enough precision without excessive width. Rounding is included as a choice since it affects accuracy at no significant area cost."
